Block: nngp_gaussian_gibbs_block
Version: 0.1.0
Date: 2026-06-30
Title: Nearest-Neighbor Gaussian Process spatial regression sampler
Description: Fits Bayesian Gaussian spatial regression with a Nearest-Neighbor
 Gaussian Process (NNGP) random effect,
 \(y_i \sim \mathcal{N}(x_i^\top \beta + w_i, \tau^2)\), where the spatial effects
 follow the sparse NNGP approximation
 \(w_i \mid w_{N(i)} \sim \mathcal{N}(b_i^\top w_{N(i)}, f_i)\) built from an
 exponential covariance \(\sigma^2 \exp(-\phi d)\) over each location's m nearest
 neighbors (KD-tree neighbor search). The coefficients \(\beta\) take a
 weakly-informative Gaussian prior, the nugget \(\tau^2\) and partial sill
 \(\sigma^2\) Inverse-Gamma priors, and the decay \(\phi\) a domain-scaled uniform
 prior. It replaces the dense \(n \times n\) GP covariance with a sparse
 neighbor-based approximation, scaling Gaussian-process spatial modeling to large
 point-referenced datasets. The effects \(w\), coefficients \(\beta\) and nugget
 \(\tau^2\) are sampled by conjugate Gibbs steps. The partial sill \(\sigma^2\) and
 decay \(\phi\) are updated jointly, and an exact parameter-expansion level shift
 improves intercept mixing. Datta, Banerjee, Finley and Gelfand (2016)
 <doi:10.1080/01621459.2015.1044091>. Finley et al. (2019)
 <doi:10.1080/10618600.2018.1537924>.
Author: Jungang Zou
Maintainer: Jungang Zou <jz3183@cumc.columbia.edu>
License: GPL-3.0-or-later
EngineKind: mcmc
ConstraintKinds: none
RoutingKey: large point-referenced spatial Gaussian process
SelectWhen: Large-scale spatial regression with Gaussian-process random effects on
 point-referenced data
Skill: skills/nngp_gaussian_gibbs_block.md
Tests: test_nngp_gaussian_gibbs_block.cpp
Depends: core (>= 1.0)
Example: examples/SpatialNNGPRegression.cpp
ExampleModel: SpatialNNGPRegression
ExampleDesc: y_i ~ Normal(x_i' beta + w_i, tau^2) with w ~ NNGP(exponential covariance sigma^2 * exp(-phi * d)), beta ~ Normal(0, sigma_beta^2), tau^2 ~ InverseGamma, sigma^2 ~ InverseGamma, and phi ~ Uniform
ExampleIntro: This example fits a spatial linear regression with Gaussian-process random effects on point-referenced data: each observation is modeled as \(y_i \sim \mathcal{N}(x_i^\top \beta + w_i,\ \tau^2)\), where \(w_i\) is a latent spatial field with an exponential covariance \(\sigma^2 \exp(-\phi d)\) approximated by a nearest-neighbor Gaussian process (NNGP) for scalability. The priors are \(\beta \sim \mathcal{N}(0, \sigma_\beta^2 I)\), inverse-gamma priors on the noise variance \(\tau^2\) and spatial variance \(\sigma^2\), and a uniform prior on the decay/range parameter \(\phi\). It demonstrates parameter recovery, a posterior-predictive check, and held-out kriging that beats a non-spatial OLS baseline.
ChecksApplicable: #15, #16, #17, BL1, BL2, BL3, BL4
ValidationSkill: skills/nngp_gaussian_gibbs_block_validation.md
